  "operatorObservations": [
    "The user foregrounded the Codex preview after earlier 1 Hz host scheduling. A separate menu clock diagnostic then observed approximately 240 Hz. All selected windows used the visible native preview panel at 1280x720 with sound muted.",
    "Each active window began from an original byte-identical imported synthetic checkpoint. The 20 and 40 labels identify starting flags, not zombie counts. No earned progress is claimed from these profiles.",
    "All four selected start and end screenshots show native active gameplay, without a pause dialog, seed chooser, flag intermission or defeat pan. No game input occurred during the timed intervals.",
    "The 1x windows used the native default with Remember Speed unchecked. The 2x windows sent the native F shortcut only after Continue had closed and the active canvas was focused. The 40/2x first end screenshot directly displayed the native 2x label; the same control sequence was used for the fresh selected 20/2x and repeated 40/2x windows.",
    "Recorder configuration was completed while paused. For fresh 20/2x, 40/1x and repeated 40/2x, arm to active start screenshot took 987, 819 and 1058 ms respectively, inside the recorder two-second delay. The first 20/1x used a fresh restored checkpoint and resume within 300 ms of arming.",
    "The separate crowded 20-flag checkpoint was used only for paused native-versus-clock controls. The original Menu remained open through both intervals.",
    "Excluded three pre-foreground 1 Hz records as scheduling-budget failures. Excluded the earlier 20/2x record because its end showed the native defeat pan and active-throughout eligibility was unproven.",
    "The first active 40/2x record met frame/native CPU limits but its three save captures took 8.7, 7.4 and 9.8 ms, exceeding the unchanged 8 ms save p95 budget. It remains failed historical evidence. One fresh repeat with the same code, fixture, settings and budgets remained active and met the bound (save p95/max 7.7 ms). This variability prevents a universal smoothness claim.",
    "No native builds, packaging or other heavy test jobs ran during the timed windows. No screenshot was taken inside a recording interval; screenshots bracket the timed windows."
  ],
  "limits": "Host preview conditions are caller-observed, not inferred from page visibility. Earlier failed diagnostic captures are retained separately; these short windows do not establish universal or GPU/presentation performance. Single-device short windows and caller-declared scenarios with screenshots. Scheduling is not delivered FPS; native callback CPU is not GPU completion timing. Future engine/shell changes require matching fresh observations.",
